ve to  prepare and for a bullet game uh of  course that's not uh  uh  you know it's easier said than done even  though this is a two plus o bullet i'm  not sure if they berserked this game uh  so you do have a little bit of an  additional time to to think uh of course  the rook could not be captured because  if you capture then this pawn is a  monster and if you recapture them bishop  d4 will will just be very scary for  example rook captures an e3 also bishop  captures an a1 so there's uh yeah there  are many many tricks in the position so  rook captures any one was played we have  rook capture sunny one and now a6 by do  both and now knight to g5 so both  players still have the bishop fare uh  and of course hikaru is hoping that he  can win the bishop pair uh  will eliminate to one of dubo's bishops  so here h6 kicking back the knight  knight to e4 now attacking the f6 bishop  and here dubo could capture on e4 and  it's a perfectly fine move but he wants  to keep the bishops in the game he plays  bishop to h4 and now knight back to g3  by hikaru uh we have queen to f6 and now  comes queen to e2 here this is a  i would say a classic uh hikaru position  as he plays uh a lot of puzzle rush and  if you if you had this position and you  had to solve it in a puzzle rush i think  he would play queen to e2 instantly uh  as it sets up a trap for duboff and you  have to  see it uh otherwise you're just dead  lost but dubois missed it uh duval  played the g6 of course you want to make  this bishop a little bit less powerful  but the this comes with a big problem so  feel free to pause the video here and  win the game for hikaru while i give you  a couple of seconds  so uh for those of you who were able to  do it congratulations on spotting that  well the rook is undefended and also uh  well the other thing uh and for those of  you who just want to enjoy the show it  is of course queen to g4 now what's the  idea here well of course you are  attacking the rook and c8 but more 